Problem:
A factory in India produces rice and corn. To make one kilogram of rice requires 2 hours of human labor, 3 hours of machine work, and 4 hours of resting under the sun. To make one kilogram of corn requires 1 hour of human labor, 5 hours of machine work, and 1 hour of resting under the sun. The factory only has 100 hours of human labor, 200 hours of machine labor, and 75 hours of time under the sun available. The net profit per kilogram of rice is $20 and the net profit per kilogram of corn is $25. How many kilograms of each should the factory make in order to maximize profit?

